  <section>
    <h2>Dispensaries in Skowhegan</h2>

    <h3>Nuggie's Cannabis</h3>
    <p><strong>Address:</strong> 12 Madison Ave, Skowhegan, ME 04976<br>
    <strong>Phone:</strong> (207) 474-9999<br>
    <strong>Hours:</strong> Mon-Sat 10am-7pm, Sun 11am-5pm<br>
    <strong>Type:</strong> Medical (MMMP)</p>
    <p>Nuggie's Cannabis is one of the central Maine dispensaries serving Somerset County's medical patients. The store offers a full medical menu — flower, vapes, edibles, concentrates, and tinctures — and is conveniently located just off the Madison Ave commercial corridor. Nuggie's draws patients from Skowhegan, Madison, Norridgewock, and the surrounding rural towns.</p>

    <h3>ReMaine Humble Farms</h3>
    <p><strong>Address:</strong> 95 E Madison Rd, Skowhegan, ME 04976<br>
    <strong>Phone:</strong> (207) 474-0000<br>
    <strong>Hours:</strong> Mon-Sat 10am-6pm<br>
    <strong>Type:</strong> Medical (MMMP) with caregiver network</p>
    <p>ReMaine Humble Farms is a medical dispensary and caregiver network rooted in Somerset County. The store carries an in-house cultivation line and partner-branded flower and concentrates. For patients throughout central Somerset, ReMaine Humble Farms functions as both a storefront and a caregiver-style supplier with deep local ties.</p>

    <h3>Terp Valley Farms — Delivery</h3>
    <p><strong>Service Area:</strong> Skowhegan, Madison, Norridgewock, Pittsfield, Hartland<br>
    <strong>Phone:</strong> (207) 431-9100<br>
    <strong>Hours:</strong> Order online, scheduled delivery windows<br>
    <strong>Type:</strong> Medical delivery (MMMP)</p>
    <p>Terp Valley Farms operates as a mobile medical dispensary serving the broader Somerset region. Patients can order online and receive scheduled home delivery, which is particularly valuable in the rural towns surrounding Skowhegan where the closest storefront may be 30 minutes away.</p>
  </section>

  <Callout title="Medical-First Market" type="insight">
    Skowhegan is part of a band of central-Maine towns that have organized their cannabis access primarily around medical delivery and caregiver networks rather than adult-use storefronts. For a population of 8,500 plus a wide rural catchment, that model works: it sidesteps the high real-estate and licensing cost of a stand-alone adult-use storefront, while still serving MMMP patients with consistent product.
  </Callout>

  <section>
    <h2>Skowhegan's Market Context</h2>
    <p>Skowhegan sits in the middle of Somerset County — a sprawling, rural county of roughly 50,000 residents spread across dozens of small towns. The town is the county seat and commercial hub, anchored by the Skowhegan State Fair (Maine's oldest agricultural fair, run annually since 1818), the Skowhegan School of Painting and Sculpture, and a downtown that has gradually reinvested in riverfront infrastructure along the Kennebec.</p>
    <p>For cannabis, Skowhegan's market is overwhelmingly medical. The town's two storefronts — Nuggie's and ReMaine Humble Farms — serve MMMP cardholders, and Terp Valley Farms' mobile delivery network extends the catchment into surrounding rural towns. Recreational shoppers typically travel east to Waterville (~20 minutes), which has a cluster of adult-use and medical dispensaries, or further south to Augusta (~45 minutes), the state capital and a major retail hub.</p>
    <p>Operators evaluating central Maine should view Skowhegan as a medical-strong, recreational-weak node within the Waterville-Augusta corridor. The two-store medical base is stable, the delivery model is well-suited to the rural catchment, and any future conversion to adult-use would likely come through an existing operator expanding their license, rather than a new entrant.</p>
  </section>

  
